  "provenance": {
    "sources": [
      "Mind's Eye Theatre: Dark Epics (WW05027), \"Nuts and Bolts\" chapter, pp.83-90 - the full mundane gear list (Melee Weapons, Throwing Weapons, Ranged Weapons, Firearms, Firearm Add-ons, Armor, Shields). Explosives (p.89-90) and \"Duration and Scope of Powers\" (p.90) are prose guidance with no printed stat entries and are not catalogued.",
      "Every entry read directly from the book's own page images (not OCR text), per reference-wod-scan-ocr-lessons."
    ],
    "tool": "read directly, 2026-10-04"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Armor has no dedicated property in world-object-schemas.php for the Health Levels it absorbs - the schema's own fields are shaped around a weapon's Bonus/Damage, not an absorbing item's own rating. `level` is otherwise unused for this book's mundane gear (it's only meaningful for Changing Breeds' fetishes, a different file), so Armor entries store Health Levels in `level` and restate it in `description`; this is a deliberate repurposing for this one book, not a schema change.",
    "`availability` is a one-entry trait_list per the design (\"Availability -> availability, one entry\"); a conditional availability line (\"Police 4, Street 3 or Underworld 2 otherwise\") is kept as the entry's own name verbatim rather than split into several entries, since the book prints it as one condition, not several independent options.",
    "A firearm's own printed `Rate` has no field of its own in the schema (not Bonus, Damage, or Special Ability) and is kept in `description` rather than folded into `powers`, which holds only the book's own \"Special Ability\" line."
  ],
